* Added keyword ``get_parameters`` to get all **Robot Framework** parameters (this includes the global ones) within the current scope.

  \"Current scope\" means: Calling ``get_parameters`` within the suite setup, will cause other results than calling ``get_parameters`` within a test.
  Within the suite setup e.g., test specific parameters like the name of the test, are not available.

  The keyword ``get_parameters`` writes all parameters to the log files and additionally returns a dictionary containing these parameters.

  It is possible to apply several filters to limit the amount of returned parameters to the desired ones only.

  **Example**:

  Import the **RobotframeworkExtensions**:

  | ``Library\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0RobotframeworkExtensions.Collection\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0WITH NAME\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0rf.extensions``

  Within a test call the keyword in this way to get all parameters with names starting with prefix ``TEST``:

  | ``$\u007btest_parameters\u007d\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0rf.extensions.get_parameters\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0startswith=TEST``

  Check of the return values:

  | ``Log Dictionary\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0${test_parameters}``

  **Output:**

  | ``+--------------------------------------------------------------------+``
  | ``¦\u00a0TESTCOUNT\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0¦\u00a0=\u00a0¦\u00a01\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0¦``
  | ``+--------------------+---+-------------------------------------------¦``
  | ``¦\u00a0TEST_DOCUMENTATION\u00a0¦\u00a0=\u00a0¦\u00a0QuickTest\u00a0documentation\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0¦``
  | ``+--------------------+---+-------------------------------------------¦``
  | ``¦\u00a0TEST_NAME\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0¦\u00a0=\u00a0¦\u00a0QuickTest\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0¦``
  | ``+--------------------+---+-------------------------------------------¦``
  | ``¦\u00a0TEST_TAGS\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0¦\u00a0=\u00a0¦\u00a0['quicktest_suite_tag',\u00a0'quick_test_tag']\u00a0¦``
  | ``+--------------------------------------------------------------------+``

  and

  | ``INFO - Dictionary size is 4 and it contains following items:``
  | ``TESTCOUNT: 1``
  | ``TEST_DOCUMENTATION: QuickTest documentation``
  | ``TEST_NAME: QuickTest``
  | ``TEST_TAGS: ['quicktest_suite_tag', 'quick_test_tag']``

  **References:**

  `RobotframeworkExtensions documentation <https://github.com/test-fullautomation/robotframework-extensions-collection/blob/develop/RobotframeworkExtensions/RobotframeworkExtensions.pdf>`_

  `Filter parameters <https://github.com/test-fullautomation/python-extensions-collection/blob/develop/PythonExtensionsCollection/PythonExtensionsCollection.pdf>`_ (section: '*String operations with CString*', method: '``StringFilter``')

  Notice: All ``StringFilter`` parameters available within ``get_parameters``, have to be written in a decapitalized format without type prefixes. Available are:
  ``\"casesensitive\"``, ``\"startswith\"``, ``\"endswith\"``, ``\"startsnotwith\"``, ``\"endsnotwith\"``, ``\"contains\"``, ``\"containsnot\"``, ``\"inclregex\"``, ``\"exclregex\"``.

  Without any filter set, all available parameters will be returned.

-----

* Added keyword ``log_parameter`` to log the value of a parameter in table format. The intention behind this is a better readibility of log files.

  * Simple data types like strings or integers are logged in a single table line.
  * Lists are logged with a separate line for every list element.
  * Dictionaries are logged with a separate line for every key.
  * Lists and dictionaries are resolved at top level only, not recursively. Every parameter value is logged in string format.
  * Every table line can be tagged with a prefix string (optional).
  * Every table can get a headline (optional).

  It is also possible to control the log level (default is ``\"INFO\"``) and if the table shall additionally be written to console or not (default is ``True``).

  **Example**:

  Import the **RobotframeworkExtensions**:

  | ``Library\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0RobotframeworkExtensions.Collection\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0WITH NAME\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0rf.extensions``

  Have a parameter available, e.g.:

  | ``*** Variables ***``
  | 
  | ``@{robot_file_param}\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0123``
  | ``...\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0456``
  | ``...\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0789``

  Call the keyword in this way:

  | ``rf.extensions.log_parameter\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0${robot_file_param}\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0parameter:\u00a0robot_file_param_3\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0parameter\u00a0headline``

  **Output:**

  | ``------------------``
  | ``parameter headline``
  | ``------------------``
  | ``╒══════════════════════════════════╤═════╕``
  | ``│ parameter: robot_file_param_3[0] │ 123 │``
  | ``├──────────────────────────────────┼─────┤``
  | ``│ parameter: robot_file_param_3[1] │ 456 │``
  | ``├──────────────────────────────────┼─────┤``
  | ``│ parameter: robot_file_param_3[2] │ 789 │``
  | ``╘══════════════════════════════════╧═════╛``

  As long as this keyword does not cause any naming conflicts, it is also possible to use a short version in **Robot Framework** style:

  | ``Log Parameter\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0${robot_file_param}\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0parameter:\u00a0robot_file_param_3\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0parameter\u00a0headline``

  **References:**

  `RobotframeworkExtensions documentation <https://github.com/test-fullautomation/robotframework-extensions-collection/blob/develop/RobotframeworkExtensions/RobotframeworkExtensions.pdf>`_
"
                                      ]
                 }
